<section class="wrap prose block">
  <h2>All combinations</h2>
  <div class="two-col pairs"><div><h3>Fire + Fire</h3><p>Two fire signs together create a lively, passionate connection full of shared energy and bold plans. You both enjoy adventure, applause and fresh starts. The friction comes when you both want to lead at once or flare up over small matters. Taking turns in the spotlight and agreeing on a common goal will help this partnership burn brightly without burning out.</p></div><div><h3>Earth + Earth</h3><p>Two earth signs together build a reliable, comfortable bond grounded in trust and practical care. You share a love of routine, quality and steady progress. The challenge is that you may both become stubborn or cautious, avoiding change even when it would help. Staying open to new experiences and telling each other what you need will keep your partnership warm and growing.</p></div><div><h3>Air + Air</h3><p>Two air signs together make for stimulating conversation, shared curiosity and plenty of laughter. You understand each other&#39;s need for variety and independence. The friction can come from too many ideas and too little follow-through, or from keeping feelings at arm&#39;s length. Making space for honest emotional talk will give your connection the depth it deserves.</p></div><div><h3>Water + Water</h3><p>Two water signs together offer deep empathy, tenderness and an intuitive understanding of each other&#39;s moods. You create a safe space for feelings and imagination. The difficulty can be moodiness or hurt feelings left unspoken, which can build up quietly. Clear, gentle communication and a few lighter, playful moments will help you stay balanced together.</p></div><div><h3>Fire + Air</h3><p>Fire and air are a stimulating pairing, as air fuels the flame and fire adds warmth to air&#39;s ideas. You inspire each other to try new things and enjoy spirited conversation. The friction may come when fire moves quickly and air wants to talk things through first. Patience and mutual respect for each other&#39;s pace will turn this combination into a dynamic, exciting partnership.</p></div><div><h3>Earth + Water</h3><p>Earth and water form a nurturing, supportive bond. Water brings emotional depth and care, while earth offers stability and practical comfort. Together you can build a secure, loving home life. The challenge is that earth may seem too pragmatic to water, and water may seem too emotional to earth. Appreciating each other&#39;s strengths will keep this partnership deeply rewarding.</p></div><div><h3>Fire + Earth</h3><p>Fire and earth bring energy and endurance together. Fire sparks ideas and enthusiasm, while earth turns them into something solid and lasting. You can accomplish a great deal side by side. The friction arises when fire wants speed and earth wants caution. Finding a shared rhythm, with room for both bold moves and careful planning, will help you thrive together.</p></div><div><h3>Air + Water</h3><p>Air and water combine curiosity with feeling, creating a connection that is both thoughtful and imaginative. Air brings lightness and fresh perspectives, while water adds depth and tenderness. The friction may appear when air seems detached and water feels misunderstood. Sharing your inner world openly and giving each other time to reflect will help you find real harmony.</p></div><div><h3>Earth + Air</h3><p>Earth and air are a practical and intellectual pairing that can be surprisingly complementary. Air brings new ideas and easy conversation, while earth offers reliability and follow-through. You can help each other grow in unexpected ways. The challenge is that air may seem restless to earth, and earth may seem rigid to air. Bringing curiosity and steadiness together makes this partnership productive and enjoyable.</p></div><div><h3>Fire + Water</h3><p>Fire and water bring passion and tenderness into one connection. Fire energises and inspires, while water soothes and understands. The attraction can be strong, though strong feelings can also clash. Fire may seem too intense to water, and water may seem too sensitive to fire. Gentle honesty and room for each other&#39;s emotional rhythm will allow this bond to feel warm and balanced.</p></div></div>
